All four findings fixed and all four gates green.

**1. BLOCKER — `network` row could not fail** (`tests/stdlib_module_names_test.rs`)
The row was `set answer to might fail network.get(...)` with expected output `None`; `might fail` discarded the `RuntimeError` and `if let Some(expected)` discarded the comparison. Proven by breaking `runtime.rs::network_get` to refuse every request — the old program still printed `ran` and exited 0. The test now owns the network: a `TcpListener` on `127.0.0.1:0` answers a fixed body, the row calls both `network.get` and `network.post` unguarded, and the table type dropped `Option` entirely (`Vec<(&str, String, String)>`) so no row can opt out. The recorded request lines (`GET /greeting`, `POST /echo`, body `ping`) are asserted too — a `network.get` changed to `.post(url)` now fails.

**2. MAJOR — cwd-relative path** (`tests/stdlib_module_names_test.rs:656`, `:679`)
`bytes.write("target/tmp/p50names/ends.bin", …)` resolved against the process cwd while the read-back used an absolute path. Both `bytes.write` programs now interpolate the absolute `scratch` path. The whole file now passes when its test binary runs from `/tmp/opencode/elsewhere`; the relative version fails there.

**3. MAJOR — `KNOWN_GAPS` was a skip-list that never expired** (`tests/stdlib_module_docs_test.rs`)
Eleven more entries were stale — `pop`, `shift`, `is_number`, `is_text`, `is_list`, `is_record`, `to_list`, `csv_parse`, `network_get`, `network_post`, `list_map` — all implemented in `src/stdlib.rs`, four asserted by name in the same file. All removed (list is now `filter`, `reduce`), and the fix is the shape: `known_gaps()` returns each name *with the program that still fails*, and the new `edge_a_known_gap_is_still_a_gap` runs them, so putting an implemented name back fails on its own. The registry walk is unchanged and still checks every registered builtin.

**4. MINOR — `Both calls block.`** (`SPEC.md:1158`)
Now names `time.sleep` as the only blocking call in § time and `network.get`/`network.post` as the other blocking calls; `time.format` and `time.unix` are pure computation per `src/runtime.rs:961`/`:981`.

Gates: `fmt` no diff · `clippy -D warnings` exit 0 · `cargo test --all-targets` **1422 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored** (53 lines, +1 = the new test) · 9 example/module files, 0 failures. No `#[ignore]`, `// skip`, `allow(clippy::)`, or deleted test; `src/runtime.rs` has no diff.
